#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:5
#: 4af566689d81404faa03eca7b2903a1c
msgid "Stabilize Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:7
#: 989a9f2aebf0450e873b62a58d92eebd
msgid "Stabilize mode allows you to fly your vehicle manually, but self-levels the roll and pitch axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:12
#: d75806d63ddf465c88fb85d35295a92a
msgid "If you're learning to fly, try :ref:`Alt Hold <altholdmode>` or :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>` instead of Stabilize. You'll have fewer crashes if you don't need to concentrate on too many controls at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:20
#: d231d4544a9d49349d74a06b48f83124
msgid "While stabilize mode does not necessarily require GPS, switching to RTL in case of emergency does. Make sure you do have a reliable position estimate prior to arming, most commonly provided by 3D GPS fix with sufficient HDOP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:25
#: 6b91db393b8449bdafa81aa4eaabeaf2
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:27
#: 13499fb0a63f40ce824a10cb34f20e3b
msgid "Pilot's roll and pitch input control the lean angle of the copter. When the pilot releases the roll and pitch sticks the vehicle automatically levels itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:30
#: 5355af57fbfa4f31962eb048c877c3a6
msgid "Pilot will need to regularly input roll and pitch commands to keep the vehicle in place as it is pushed around by the wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:32
#: 8c4637aa2e8c427b9376cb594f8b3af6
msgid "Pilot's yaw input controls the rate of change of the heading.  When the pilot releases the yaw stick the vehicle will maintain its current heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:35
#: 611f5412300841ab9bfd397c96450f8c
msgid "Pilot's throttle input controls the average motor speed meaning that constant adjustment of the throttle is required to maintain altitude.  If the pilot puts the throttle completely down the motors will go to their minimum rate (:ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>`) and if the vehicle is flying it will lose attitude control and tumble. However, this behavior can be changed by enabling :ref:`airmode`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:41
#: 8a419248e2df4ce49c56220e2bec0f9a
msgid "The throttle sent to the motors is automatically adjusted based on the tilt angle of the vehicle (i.e. increased as the vehicle tilts over more) to reduce the compensation the pilot must do as the vehicle's attitude changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:48
#: e1b97e53f622432bac9ab121e0b39268
msgid "Always switch into a manual mode such as stabilize if the autopilot fails to control the vehicle. Maintaining control of your copter is your responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:53
#: 43d636ee2b1d416cbed283ad159f9423
msgid "AirMode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:55
#: af527fc6782d4c3ebb520b949776c98b
msgid "Stabilize mode can be setup to provide full stabilization at idle throttle. See :ref:`airmode`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:60
#: 9e370cef640141a1931a8e5e49c64df6
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:62
#: 9861c404f4674d2a9b1a2f57aa6be8d0
msgid "See :ref:`common-tuning` for complete tuning topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:64
#: 7080b7b8b0bb43e6bc91133f35106296
msgid "Using :ref:`AutoTune <autotune>` may allow you to automatically determine the best Stabilize and Rate PID values. It is highly suggested running AutoTune on your vehicle rather than manually adjusting PIDs. However, see :ref:`ac_rollpitchtuning` for roll and pitch manual tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:68
#: f5bcf9879a1c4e78b184e384babbaf19
msgid "Other important parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:69
#: bf38e7ba6a904a4aa1bf7fd7a402b349
msgid ":ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>` controls the maximum lean angle which by default is 30 (i.e. 30 degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:71
#: dfbe12201d1a4914a2316fcb500a6e83
msgid ":ref:`PILOT_Y_RATE<PILOT_Y_RATE>` controls the maximum yaw rate requested by a pilot's yaw input in Stabilize and other pilot-controlled modes except Acro. Higher values request a faster yaw rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:74
#: 34effdc3a83d4664a2602d029c1374b9
msgid ":ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` can be used to control the responsiveness to changes in pitch and roll angles requested by pilot's inputs."
msgstr ""
